[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 2"""
 date="2026-11-08T23:48:18Z"
 content="""
Refinement: The AnnexWorkerPool is already a bounded pool of Annex objects,
so lift it out of PerRepoServerState so there is a single bounded pool.

This would let --jobs control the total number of worker threads across all
repositories served. An especially active repository would get more worker
threads actively running. And helper processes, started by the worker
threads, would be limited to a small multiple of --jobs.

Question: PerRepoServerState also has an annexState and annexRead that are
not part of the AnnexWorkerPool so would not be affected by that. 
Are those used anywhere that spawns helper processes?
"""]]
